{"text":"entities by name. An ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"add hook","type":"text"}]},{"text":" runs when an entity that didn’t hold a ","type":"text"},{"code":"C","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" gets one, by","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"spawning, inserting or applying a command. Replacing a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"C"},{"type":"text","text":" the entity already holds"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"doesn’t run it; see "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/onInsert(_:perform:)"},{"text":" for a hook that runs then too.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The following example records each named entity in a resource as it’s spawned:"}]},{"code":["struct NameDirectory: Resource { var entities: [String: Entity] = [:] }","","var world = World()","world.resources.insert(NameDirectory())","world.onAdd(Name.self) { world, entity in","    let name = world[Name.self, of: entity].value","    world.resources[NameDirectory.self].entities[name] = entity","}","","let hero = world.spawn(Name(value: \"Hero\"))","print(world.resources[NameDirectory.self].entities[\"Hero\"] == hero)","\/\/ Prints \"true\""],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A hook runs after the world operation that fired it has finished, so it sees every","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"component a spawn or bundle insert gave. Hooks run in the order they were fired. A change"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that a hook makes fires hooks of its own, which run after the hooks already waiting."}]},{"type":"aside","name":"Note","style":"note","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Changes made in place, through the world’s subscript or an update, run no hooks.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"te